== Knowledge continuum ==
BITwiki is the durable semantic knowledge layer. BIThub is the live collaboration/work layer. BITCORE is the cognition and orchestration layer.

Useful work can be researched, tested, corrected, and shaped in BIThub; processed through human and AI workflows; preserved as reusable artifacts; and crystallized into BITwiki when stable enough.

'''Useful intelligence should compound.'''

== Notice ==
'''WIP / evolving corpus:''' BITwiki contains human-assisted AI material and historical experimental content. Important claims should be verified against sources. V2 is actively reconciling the public V1 corpus without silently rewriting unrecovered pages.

